2026-05-03 13:03:14 [nitro@ryzen5] now need to fix accept on slopfountain side
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] Looking at `slopprompt.ts`, the accept logic for incoming connections is incomplete. The
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] `listenService` creates listeners but never starts accepting. In `slopPrompt`, you race against
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] `listenerPromise` but that variable is never set. The `acceptAll` function exists but is not
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] called. Below is a fixed version of the accept flow.
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] • Problem*
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] Listeners are created (`sloppyListener`, `riffListener`, `foggyListener`) but no accept promise is
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] stored in `listenerPromise`. Consequently, the race in `slopPrompt` never sees incoming connections
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] and `listenerPromise` remains `undefined`.
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] • Solution*
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] - Replace `listenService` with a function that both creates listeners and starts the accept cycle,
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] returning a promise that resolves with `{connection, name, port}`.
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] - Remove the old `acceptAll` and integrate a single `acceptListener` loop that re‑arms itself after
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] each connection.
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] - In `slopPrompt`, use that promise in the race, handle the connection, and set up the next accept.
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:38 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
