2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] When a connection arrives, handle it as before but also set up reading from that connection:
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] if (winner.connection) {
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 	const { connection, name } = winner;
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 	slopConnections.set(name, connection);
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 	const receiver = readNamedConnection(name, connection);
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 	receivePromises[name] = receiver;
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 	continue;
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] Why this works
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] - Each listener gets its own accept promise that self‑re‑arms after the first connection.
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] - The race sees all accept promises and whichever resolves first is handled.
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] - Connections are read via `readNamedConnection` and stored in `receivePromises`, which are also
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] raced in the loop.
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] This fixes the missing accept loop and makes the slop fountain side listen correctly for incoming
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] bot connections.
2026-05-03 13:03:39 [deepseek-v4] 
