2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] Here's a modular fix for `slopprompt.ts` that replaces the broken accept logic with a clean,
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] extensible listener registry.
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] • Key changes*
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 1. Remove the old `sloppyPromise/riffPromise/listenerPromise`, `slopListener[]`,
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] `slopPortName{}`, `listenPort()`, `acceptPort()`, `acceptAll()`.
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 2. Add a `Map<string, ListenerEntry>` where each entry holds the `Deno.Listener` and an
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] auto‑re‑arming accept promise.
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 3. Export `startListener(name, port)` so bots can register themselves.
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 4. Rewrite `listenService()` to use `startListener` for the three default ports.
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 5. Update `slopPrompt` to collect all accept promises from the registry and race them.
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 6. Remove the `sloppyPort/riffPort/foggyPort` assignments inside `slopPrompt` (they are now
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] handled by the registry).
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] // Replace the messy globals:
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] // Global listener registry – modular, extensible
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] interface ListenerEntry {
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 	listener: Deno.Listener;
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 	acceptPromise: Promise<{ connection: Deno.TcpConn; name: string; port: number }>;
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] const listenerRegistry = new Map<string, ListenerEntry>();
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] // ---- Listen port management ----
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:25:53 [deepseek-v4] async function acceptLoop(
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] 	listener: Deno.Listener,
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] 	name: string,
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] 	port: number
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] ): Promise<{ connection: Deno.TcpConn; name: string; port: number }> {
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] 	const connection = await listener.accept();
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] 	// Re‑arm the accept promise immediately
2026-05-03 13:25:54 [deepseek-v4] 	listenerRegistry.set(name, {
