2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for sharing these source files. I have reviewed the three primary modules (`relay.ts`,
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] `slopprompt.ts`, `sloppybot.ts`) and the smaller `slopsearch.ts`. This appears to be a research
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] tool ("Slop Relay / Fountain") for interacting with multiple large language models from a terminal,
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] with Discord integration and experimental networking.
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] The overall architecture is clear: a central relay that routes chat history to various LLM backends
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] (OpenAI, DeepSeek, Google, Anthropic) via a common `ChatCompletion` interface, while
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] `slopprompt.ts` provides raw-mode input with shortcode expansion and `sloppybot.ts` acts as a
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] Discord bridge.
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] Some notable design choices and features:
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] - Model routing via `@account` suffix, with per-model pricing, temperature, tool-use, and
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] thinking budget controls.
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] - Tool (function calling) relay – correct recursive handling of tool results across
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] providers.
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] - Slop broadcast / listen services – TCP-based interprocess messaging (ports 8081-8083) for
2026-05-03 13:44:02 [deepseek-v4] composable microservices.
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] - Unicode width handling – custom `stringWidth` and `discordStringWidth` to account for
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] variable-width emoji and CJK characters, important for terminal tables and Discord message
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] formatting.
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] - Gemini TTS integration via `geminiSay` and WAV generation – a non-trivial addition.
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] - History management – save/load/reset/push/pop of session histories, with squashing of
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] consecutive same-role messages.
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] - “Slopmark” timestamps – hex encoding of 16ths of a second since a baseline date, used for
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] logging and ordering.
2026-05-03 13:44:03 [deepseek-v4] 
