2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] `[SLOPPY] discordClient online <bot name>`. If not, either the token is missing (env `DISCORD_BOT`)
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] or the bot is not invited to the server.
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] 2. Are the TCP ports free?
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    The fountain (relay) listens on 8081, 8082, 8083 when `listen` config flag is enabled. The bot
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] connects to port 8081 by default.
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    Run `netstat -an | findstr :8081` (Windows) or `lsof -i :8081` (macOS/Linux) to see if something
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] is already listening.
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    If you start the fountain after the bot (or vice versa), you’ll get `Address already in use`
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] errors (check stderr of both processes).
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] 3. Logs from the bot (sloppybot)
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    It writes debug messages to `console.error` (splurt). Look for lines like:
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    - `connected with noDelay localhost:8081` – connection succeeded.
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    - `Connection Refused` – the fountain is not listening yet.
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4]    - `Connection Error` – something else (e.g., firewall, port blocked).
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:01 [deepseek-v4] 4. Logs from the fountain
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]    When a TCP client connects, `slopprompt.ts` prints:
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]    `[PROMPT] listening for slop <port> <name>`
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]    and later:
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]    `connection received for <name>`
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]    If you see these, the link is up.
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] Common pitfalls
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] - Double‑listen in `slopprompt.ts`
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]   In `slopPrompt()` it calls `listenPort(8081...)` again, even if `listenService()` already opened
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] the port. This will fail silently (or throw) because the port is already bound. I recommend
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] removing the listen calls inside `slopPrompt` – the listeners should only be created once, either
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] in `listenService()` or inside `slopPrompt`, not both.
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] - Bot‑fountain ordering
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]   The bot waits 20 seconds before trying to connect. If the fountain starts later, the bot will
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] keep retrying (only once, unfortunately). Consider adding a reconnection loop in
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] `connectFountain()`.
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] - Firewall / antivirus
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]   On Windows, Deno may need explicit permission to listen on localhost ports. Check Windows
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] Defender notifications.
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] - Missing `listen` config flag
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4]   In `relay.ts`, `listenService()` and `acceptThread()` are only called if `roha.config.listen` is
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] true. Make sure you set that flag (e.g., `/config listen` command) before trying to use the bot.
2026-05-03 13:56:02 [deepseek-v4] 
