2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] type conn.txt | nc localhost 8081
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] If the fountain receives this, you should see the message appear in its output (as a line push to
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] the model). If it does, the problem is on the bot side.
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] 5. Possible code bug: double listen
2026-05-03 13:57:13 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] As mentioned earlier, `slopPrompt()` calls `listenPort(8081,...)` even though `listenService()`
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] already bound those ports. That will throw `Address already in use`. The error is silently caught
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] in `listenPort` (it returns `{error: error}` but the caller ignores it). That means the second
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] listen is silently failing, but the first one (from `listenService`) is still working. So the
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] server is up, but the bot connects to a listener that is actually the first one. That’s fine.
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] But inside `slopprompt.ts`, the `slopPrompt` function overwrites `sloppyPromise`, `riffPromise`,
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] etc. This could cause race conditions – the `slopPrompt` listeners are only used inside that
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] function; the main relay’s `acceptThread` is separate and uses its own listeners. That duplication
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] is messy but shouldn’t prevent operation.
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] Recommended fix
2026-05-03 13:57:14 [deepseek-v4] 
