2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] Overall Structure
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] - Well-modularized – Separates console input handling (`slopprompt.ts`), Discord
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] integration (`sloppybot.ts`), web search (`slopsearch.ts`), and the core `relay.ts`.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] - TypeScript used with Deno, using ES modules and JSR/npm dependencies.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] - Custom emoji/Unicode style – Heavy use of decorative Unicode characters, custom
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] shortcodes, and wide/narrow glyph handling.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] Key Design Patterns
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] 1. Recursive relay loop – `relay` function recursively processes tool calls, then continues
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] the conversation. This is a clean pattern for handling multi-turn function calls.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] 2. History management – `rohaHistory` array with push/pop session stack; `squashMessages`
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] to merge consecutive same-role entries.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] 3. Multi‑provider adapter – Each provider (OpenAI, DeepSeek, Google, Anthropic) has its own
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] connection/chat method via `connectAccount()` and a unified `chat.completions.create` interface.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] 4. File sharing – `shareSlop`, `commitShares`, `shareBlob` handle local file scanning,
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] dedup by hash, and attaching as text/images to the conversation.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] Potential Issues / Notes
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] - Error handling in `relay` – Many `catch` blocks return `spend` early but do not rethrow
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] or signal failure to the caller. This could mask API errors.
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] - Performance – The `readNamedConnection` and `receivePromises` map may leak entries if
2026-05-04 08:14:05 [deepseek-v4] clients disconnect without proper cleanup (though you do delete on error).
