2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for sharing these files. The Slop Relay system is an impressive, many:many research tool
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] for interacting with multiple LLM providers. I’ve reviewed the core relay, prompt handler, Discord
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] bots, and the session log.
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] A few observations:
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 1. Architecture – The relay runs as a Deno process that connects to several API providers
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] (DeepSeek, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, xAI, etc.) via accounts.json. It maintains a shared
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] conversation history (`rohaHistory`) and broadcasts output to Discord bots through a local TCP
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] server. This setup allows you to flip between models mid‑session.
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 2. Prompt handling – `slopprompt.ts` implements raw‑mode input with shortcode replacement,
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] grapheme‑aware backspace, and history navigation. It also manages multiple bot connections using
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] `Promise.race`. This is a clever way to interleave keyboard input, incoming bot messages, and timer
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] ticks without blocking.
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 3. Discord bots – Each bot (`foggy`, `sloppy`, `riff`) connects to the local relay and
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] relays messages to/from a Discord channel. The output log shows all three bots connected and
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] successfully passing a user query (“<@&…> you good?”) to the DeepSeek model and broadcasting the
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] reply.
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] 4. Session metadata – The status line printed after each relay call includes model name,
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] temperature, cost, history size, and elapsed time. This is useful for tracking usage across
2026-05-05 10:05:50 [deepseek-v4] different models.
