2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] The `output2.txt` log confirms the pattern: when a user sends a message from Discord, the `from`
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] field is set to the Discord username (e.g., `"scudmarks@discord"`). The relay echoes that with a `>
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] >` prefix using `from: "friend"` (the `rohaNic`). Then the model replies with `from: "🐋"` (the
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] DeepSeek emoji), and the status line goes out with `from: "slop"`.
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] So the possible `from` values you'll see are exactly:
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] - Discord username (e.g., `"scudmarks@discord"`) – raw user message forwarded by the bot.
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] - `rohaNic` (e.g., `"friend"`) – the relay's echoed user query.
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] - Provider emoji (e.g., `"🐋"`) – the model's response.
2026-05-05 10:15:09 [deepseek-v4] - `"slop"` – internal console/status messages.
