2026-05-05 10:17:09 [nitro@ryzen5] the models response is assigned where?
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] The model response’s `from` field is assigned at the point where `slopBroadcast` is called in the
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] `relay` function. In `relay.ts`, after a successful completion, you’ll find this pattern (around
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] line 1400‑1500):
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] const config = modelAccounts[account];
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] const emoji = config ? (config.emoji || "") : "";
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] // … later, after building the reply content …
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] rohaHistory.push({role:"assistant", mut, emoji, name:model, content, elapsed, price:spend});
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] slopBroadcast(content, emoji);
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] The second argument to `slopBroadcast`—`emoji`—becomes the `from` field in the JSON message sent to
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] the bots. That emoji is drawn from the `emoji` property of the account configuration in
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] `accounts.json` (e.g., `"🐋"` for DeepSeek). So the `from` value for a model reply is the
2026-05-05 10:17:16 [deepseek-v4] provider’s account emoji.
