2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] Ah, you mean even though logging is `true`, the `[from]` tag doesn't appear in `forge.log`. Let's
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] trace why.
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] The `logForge` call in `chat()` is:
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] logForge(content, m.from);
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] Inside `logForge`:
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] async function logForge(lines: string, id: string) {
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 	if (roha.config.logging) {
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 		const time = slopmark();
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 		const list = [];
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 		for (let line of lines.split("\n")) {
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 			line = stripAnsi(line);
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 			line = time + " [" + id + "] " + line + "\n";
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 			list.push(line);
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 		}
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 		let path = resolve(forgePath, "forge.log");
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 		await Deno.writeTextFile(path, list.join("\n"), { append: true });
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 	}
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] If `roha.config.logging` is `true`, each line should be written with `[scudmarks@discord]` prefix.
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] So why wouldn't you see it? Possible reasons:
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 1. `m.from` is undefined – if the message object doesn't have a `from` field. But from the
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] `output.txt` we see the JSON includes `"from":"scudmarks@discord"`, so it should be there.
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 2. The log file path is different – `forgePath` is `C:\nitrologic\relay\forge`, so the file
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] would be `C:\nitrologic\relay\forge\forge.log`. Are you looking in the right file? The `forge.log`
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] might be overwritten or appended. Could you check the actual log file content?
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 3. `roha.config.logging` was false when those messages arrived and you toggled it later –
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] logging only writes from the moment it's enabled. If you turned it on after the messages, they
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] won't appear.
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 4. The `logForge` call doesn't happen for Discord messages – In `chat()`, the block
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] receiving `response.messages` calls `logForge(content, m.from)`. But what if the `m.message` object
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] doesn't have a `from` field? Let's examine the `slopprompt.ts` return:
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] if (blob.messages) {
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4]     for (const message of blob.messages) {
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4]         messages.push({ message, from: message.from });
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4]     }
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] Here `message` is the object `{message: "...", from: "..."}`, so `m.message` becomes that object.
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] Then in `chat()` you do:
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] const content = m.message.content || m.message.message || JSON.stringify(m.message) || "<nocontent>";
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:35:09 [deepseek-v4] 
