2026-05-05 10:38:16 [nitro@ryzen5] verbose logging should not end up on discord
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] You're right – when `verbose` is on, many debug `echo()` calls end up in `outputBuffer`, which then
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] goes to `flush()`, and `flush()` sends everything to `slopBroadcast`, meaning Discord bots echo
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] those debug lines back into the Discord channel. That's noisy and unwanted.
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] • The fix: introduce a dedicated `echoVerbose()` function that only outputs to the terminal
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] console and `forge.log`, not* to the Discord broadcast. Then replace all places where you
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] currently use `echo()` for debug/verbose messages with `echoVerbose()`.
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] Implementation
2026-05-05 10:38:30 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] Add this new function near `echoInfo` / `echo`:
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] function echoVerbose(...args: any[]): void {
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	if (!roha.config.verbose) return;
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	const lines = [];
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	for (const arg of args) {
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 		lines.push(toString(arg).trimEnd());
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	}
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	const output = lines.join(" ").trimEnd();
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	if (output.length) {
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 		console.log(output); // only to console
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 		// optional: also log to file if logging is on
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 		logForge(output, "verbose");
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 	}
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] Then change all calls like:
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] if (roha.config.verbose) echo("details ...");
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] to:
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] echoVerbose("details ...");
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] For example, in `relay.ts`:
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] - In `relay()` function, the `echoInfo` about usage, cached, balance – these are currently being
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] broadcasted.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] - In `commitShares`, `debugValue`, `echoInfo` inside `if(verbose)` blocks.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] - In `bumpModel`, etc.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] • Crucially:* keep `echo()` only for user‑visible messages that should appear in Discord
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] (like model responses, status lines, errors). Debug statements like "details spend", "usage",
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] "cached tokens" go to `echoVerbose()` instead.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] Result
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] - Console: you see all verbose output as before.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] - `forge.log`: verbose lines are still written.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] - Discord: only the important user‑facing messages appear.
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] Would you like me to provide the exact patch for the first few key places (e.g., in `relay()` and
2026-05-05 10:38:31 [deepseek-v4] `bumpModel()`)?
