2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] Based on your shared session, I see a few significant problems in the relay system that cause
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] degraded operation:
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] • 1. Unnecessary raw byte echo broadcasts to all bots*
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] In `slopprompt.ts`, `readNamedConnection` logs raw byte arrays via `echo()`:
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] echo("[STATUS] readNamedConnection",name,n,bytes);
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] This `echo()` goes through the output buffer and gets broadcast to all connected slop clients. You
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] can see the effect in `output2.txt`:
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] [STATUS] readNamedConnection connection0 88 123,34,109,101,115,115,97,103,101,115,34,58,91...
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] This should use `echoInfo()` instead, which bypasses the broadcast pipeline.
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] • 2. Stale receive promises accumulate without cleanup*
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] In `slopprompt.ts`, `receivePromises[name]` is set after each read but never removed on error or
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] disconnection:
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] receivePromises[name] = receiver;
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] When a connection returns `source` (either success or error), the promise is overwritten but the
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] connection object may be invalid. The `delete receivePromises[name]` call only runs in the success
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] path. If the connection errors, the throw at line:
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] throw(error); // this will cause a crash
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] terminates the entire prompt loop, bringing down the relay.
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] • 3. Connection error handling throws instead of recovering*
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] When a bot connection has an error, `readNamedConnection` returns `{source: connection, error,
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] name}`, but the handler in `slopPrompt` throws rather than cleaning up and retrying.
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] • 4. Duplicate echoInfo calls on every bot read*
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] In `relay.ts`, the `readNamedConnection` line:
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] echo("[STATUS] readNamedConnection", name, n, bytes);
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] logs twice for the same message — once with `readNamedConnection 90 connection0` (just name and
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] length) and once with the full byte dump. The two log statements appear in different places in the
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] code.
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:28 [deepseek-v4] • 5. `remoteBuffer` processes stale entries silently*
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] In `relay.ts`, `remoteBuffer` collects overridden `console.error` calls. The flush function
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] processes them:
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] for (const {line, from} of remoteBuffer) {
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     // muted on public channels
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     //      send.push(line);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     // dont share just log remote chatter
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     //      rohaPush(line,from);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     await logForge(line,from);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] The code says "dont share" but still writes every error to forge.log. This can fill the log quickly
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] with chatter messages that should be filtered.
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] • Suggested fixes:*
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] For issue 1 — change `echo` to `echoInfo` in `readNamedConnection`:
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] if (n == null) {
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     echoInfo("[STATUS] readNamedConnection close", name);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     return {source: connection};
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] echoInfo("[STATUS] readNamedConnection bytes", name, n);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] For issue 2 — clean up on both success and error paths, and remove the throw:
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] if (source) {
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     delete receivePromises[name];
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     if (error) {
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]         echoInfo("[PROMPT] connection error", name, error.message);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]         slopConnections.delete(name);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]         continue;
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     }
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     // ... process receive data ...
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] For issue 5 — filter `remoteBuffer` to exclude connection chatter:
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] for (const {line, from} of remoteBuffer) {
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     if (line.includes("readNamedConnection") || line.includes("connection")) continue;
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4]     await logForge(line, from);
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] The system is fundamentally working — messages flow from Discord through to the model and back. But
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] these debug-logging and error-handling issues create noise and risk crashes.
2026-05-05 14:13:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] I see you've applied the first fix (using `echoInfo` for `readNamedConnection`). Now let's address
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] the remaining issues.
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] • Problem 2: error handling throws instead of cleaning up*
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] Current code:
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4] if(error){
2026-05-05 14:16:29 [deepseek-v4]     echo("[PROMPT] oh no error from",name,error.message);
