2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for sharing these files. The relay system is an impressive many:many user-model
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] architecture. Here are some observations:
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] - Provider integration is broad—DeepSeek, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, plus local
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] accounts—and the `connectAccount` pattern keeps extension clean.
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] - TCP-based `slopBroadcast` provides real-time message passing to Discord bots (riff,
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] sloppy, foggy), each with distinct roles. The raw-mode prompt loop `slopPrompt` manages concurrent
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] I/O from keyboard, listener, and bot connections.
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] - Tool call handling with recursion in `relay()` allows multi-turn function usage (e.g.,
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] `readtime`, `submitfile`). The `rohaHistory` structure tracks cost, elapsed time, and
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] reasoning content per message.
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] - Code style uses tabs and minimal whitespace as specified. Heavy reliance on `console.log`
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] for output—consider migrating to a structured logging approach for production use.
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] - The `output` logs show live interaction: bot registrations, a test exchange with deepseek, and
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] cost tracking.
2026-05-05 14:27:16 [deepseek-v4] 
