2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] - The `relay.ts` ⇄ `slopprompt.ts` ⇄ `slopbot.ts` triad is a nice separation: relay owns model
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] state, slopprompt owns raw stdin + the bot socket on 8081, and each slopbot is a thin Discord shim.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] The `Promise.race([readPromise, timerPromise, listenerPromise, ...receivers])` loop in `slopPrompt`
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] is the heart of it and it reads cleanly.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] - NDJSON-over-TCP between relay and bots is a sensible choice. The `}\n{` split in `slopbot.ts
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] onFountain` is the fragile bit — if a single `read()` ever lands mid-frame you'll mis-parse. A
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] persistent line buffer on the bot side would harden it.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] • A few things that jumped out as possibly buggy* (just flagging, no code unless you want
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] it):
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 1. `slopbot.ts` reads `Deno.args[2] || 8081` as `portNumber` but it's a string when supplied via
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] CLI; `Deno.connect({port})` wants a number. Works because your task hardcodes `8081`, but
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] `connectFountain(portNumber)` would silently fail with a string from args.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 2. `slopbot.ts` references `onSystem` and `readSystem` in the main race loop — neither is defined
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] in the file you shared. If `result.system` ever fired it'd throw.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 3. `slopprompt.ts` `announceCommand` iterates `for (const connection of slopConnections)` but
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] `slopConnections` is a `Map`, so `connection` would be a `[name, conn]` tuple, not the conn.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] `slopBroadcast` does it correctly with `for (const [name, connection] of slopConnections)`.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 4. `relay.ts` `try { ` ``` ` switch(words[0]) {` — that stray backtick-pair after `try {` looks
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] like a leftover and would be a syntax error… except TypeScript parses ` `` ` as an empty template
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] literal expression statement, so it survives. Harmless but odd.
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] 5. In `relay.ts` `bumpModel`, `spent3[1]` is being treated as cached tokens, but the `spent3` array
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] constructed at the responses-endpoint call site is `[inputtokens, cached, outputtokens]`
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] whereas the legacy path computes `spent[0..1]` as `[prompt, completion]` with cached pulled
2026-05-06 09:28:22 [claude-opus-4-7] separately. Works, just two different conventions living next to each other.
