2026-05-06 09:29:58 [claude-opus-4-7] The whale 🐋 comes from `modelAccounts[provider].emoji` in `accounts.json`. Tracing where it gets
2026-05-06 09:29:58 [claude-opus-4-7] attached to outbound messages in `relay.ts`:
2026-05-06 09:29:58 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:58 [claude-opus-4-7] • 1. Resolved in `relay()`* (near the top):
2026-05-06 09:29:58 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] const config=modelAccounts[account];
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] const emoji=config?(config.emoji||""):"";
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] • 2. Used in three places inside `relay()`:*
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] - Broadcast to bots (responses endpoint path):
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   slopBroadcast(emoji+" "+content, from);
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   …but the second arg is `from`, not the emoji — so the emoji is prepended to the message
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] body.
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] - Broadcast to bots (legacy chat completions path):
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   const content2="\n### "+content;
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   slopBroadcast(content2, emoji);   // <-- here emoji IS the `from`
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   This is the one that produces the `"from":"🐋"` you see in `output.txt`/`output2.txt`. The `### `
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] is what makes Discord render the reply as a header.
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] - Status line:
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   const modelSpec=[rohaTitle, rohaModel, emoji, forge, temp, cost, size, elapsed.toFixed(2)+"s"];
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7]   Producing the ` ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.1 ⛲  deepseek-v4 🐋 🪠 0.7° …` line.
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] • 3. Stored on the history item:*
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] rohaHistory.push({role:"assistant", mut, emoji, name:model, content, elapsed, price:spend});
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] So `item.emoji` is later available to `logHistory()` (which prints `item.emoji+" "+price` in the
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] log row).
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] • 4. Also used in `modelCommand` / `onAccount`* for the model and credit tables (the brand
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] column).
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] • Inconsistency worth noting:* the two `slopBroadcast` call sites disagree about whether
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] the emoji is the `from` field or part of the message:
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] - responses path → `slopBroadcast(emoji+" "+content, from)` → bots see `from: "friend"` (or
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] whatever)
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] - legacy path → `slopBroadcast("\n### "+content, emoji)` → bots see `from: "🐋"`
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] Your `output.txt` only shows the legacy path, which is why everything is attributed to
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] `"from":"🐋"`. If you ever switch a model onto the responses endpoint you'll get a different
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] attribution shape on the Discord side.
2026-05-06 09:29:59 [claude-opus-4-7] 
