2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] Key observations:
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] - Architecture: The main application (`relay.ts`) manages a shared conversation history as
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] an array of `Plop` objects, routes prompts to the currently selected model, and handles tool call
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] loops recursively. A separate service (`slopprompt.ts`) provides raw‑mode input, remote connections
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] (TCP port 8081), and short‑code expansion. Discord bots (`slopbot.ts`) connect to the relay via TCP
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] to bridge Discord messages.
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] - Model Management: Accounts and pricing are configured in `accounts.json` and
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] `modelspecs.json`. Models are discovered on startup by querying each provider’s API. The active
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] model can be switched via `/model` in the CLI. Pricing is tracked in `roha.lode` (per‑account
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] credit) and `roha.mut` (per‑model usage).
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] - File Sharing: Users can share files or directories with `/share`, and commit them to
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] context with `/push` or `/commit`. Supported types include images (base64) and text. The relay also
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] supports tool calls for `readtime`, `submitfile`, `fetchfile`, and `tagslop`.
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] - Output Handling: Markdown is rendered to ANSI (with a custom `mdToAnsi` function), tables
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] are drawn with Unicode box‑drawing characters, and long content is chunked for Discord. A `flush()`
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] function aggregates output, logs it, and broadcasts to connected Discord bots.
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] - Unicode & Emoji: Extensive support for emoji, wide characters, and hieroglyphs is
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] provided via `slopspec.json` and `shortcode.json`. The `stringWidth` and `discordStringWidth`
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] functions account for platform‑specific display widths.
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] - Potential Improvements:
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4]   - The code is monolithic (128k in `relay.ts`); breaking it into modules would improve
2026-05-07 11:38:12 [deepseek-v4] maintainability.
