2026-05-07 15:12:46 [gemini-3.1-lite] A note on the RP2350
2026-05-07 15:12:46 [gemini-3.1-lite] Since you are using the Pico 2, keep in mind that the PIO blocks on the RP2350 have a "clock
2026-05-07 15:12:46 [gemini-3.1-lite] divider" feature. If you ever find that your `[n]` delay slots are not enough to reach a specific
2026-05-07 15:12:46 [gemini-3.1-lite] timing, you can adjust the `smconfigset_clkdiv` in your C code to slow down the entire
2026-05-07 15:12:46 [gemini-3.1-lite] state machine by a fractional amount, which can sometimes make timing calculations cleaner.
2026-05-07 15:12:46 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
