2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] Why this is the optimal approach:
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  Bit-to-Phase Mapping: With `div = 9.3885`, your PIO clock is exactly 17.734475\text MHz
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] (4 × 4.43361875\text MHz).
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  Cycle Accuracy:
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `out pins, 1 [1]` = 2 cycles.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `jmp x-- loop` = 1 cycle.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Total = 3 cycles.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Wait, since you have 4 bits per cycle, you are outputting 1 bit every 3 cycles. This
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] results in a sample rate of 17.734475 / 3 = 5.91\text MHz.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  The "Oops" Correction: Since you are outputting 1 bit every 3 cycles, you are actually
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] outputting slightly more than 4 bits per subcarrier cycle. To get exactly 4 bits per subcarrier
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] cycle at that clock rate, you need your loop to take 4 cycles total.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] The 4-Cycle Loop Modification
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] To make your bit-train perfectly align with the color subcarrier (4 bits per cycle):
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] loop:
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     out pins, 1 [2]    ; 1 + 2 = 3 cycles
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     jmp x-- loop [0]   ; 1 cycle (total 4)
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite]     set pins, 0
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] • With this change:*
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Each `out` instruction occurs once every 4 PIO cycles.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Since your clock is set to 4 × f_sc, each bit lasts exactly 1/4 of a color subcarrier cycle.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] • This gives you perfect quadrature alignment.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] Final sanity check on your logic:
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] • 8 bits from FIFO: Since each bit is 1/4 of a cycle, 8 bits = 2 full cycles of the
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] subcarrier.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Alignment: Because the PIO is now perfectly phase-locked to the subcarrier clock, your
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] "Red" bit patterns (`0xCC` and `0x33`) will stay rock-solid on the screen without any drifting.
2026-05-07 15:33:14 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
