2026-05-07 15:36:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] The addition of the 68pF capacitor and the extra 100Ω resistor in your second
2026-05-07 15:36:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] CHROMA design is a very good idea. You are essentially building a low-pass reconstruction
2026-05-07 15:36:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] filter.
2026-05-07 15:36:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:36:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] Why you should definitely add the extra components:
2026-05-07 15:36:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  Harmonic Suppression: As we discussed, a 1-bit PIO output is a square wave. A square
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] wave is mathematically a sum of the fundamental frequency (4.43\text MHz) and many odd harmonics
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] (13.3\text MHz, 22.1\text MHz, etc.). Without the filter, those harmonics will create "ghosting" or
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] high-frequency noise on your Luma signal.
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  Impedance Matching: The 100Ω and 68pF form an RC filter that rounds off the sharp edges
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] of your square wave. This turns the "stepped" signal into a much cleaner sine-like wave, which is
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] exactly what a PAL receiver expects for the color subcarrier.
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  Cross-Talk Reduction: The extra 330Ω resistor acts as a voltage divider, ensuring the
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] Chroma amplitude doesn't overwhelm the Luma signal.
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] Recommendation: Go with the "CHROMA2" version.
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] The additional components will significantly improve your image quality. Here is why the specific
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] values are good:
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] • 68pF: At 4.43\text MHz, X_c = 1 / (2 π f C) \approx 528\Omega. This, combined with your
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 100Ω/330Ω resistors, creates a gentle roll-off that preserves the subcarrier while suppressing the
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] digital switching noise.
2026-05-07 15:36:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
