2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] A Pro-Tip for the 2-Pin Hardware
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Pin A (High weight): Connect to the 100Ω resistor.
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Pin B (Low weight): Connect to the 330Ω resistor.
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • By toggling both, you get a 4-level DAC (0, 1, 2, 3).
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • The Pattern: For a sine wave, you would push patterns like `00, 01, 11, 10` into the
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] FIFO. This will look like a "staircase" that the filter will smooth into a beautiful,
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] low-distortion subcarrier.
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • This is a significant step up in signal quality.* By using the 2-pin approach, you
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] essentially eliminate the high-frequency switching noise that usually plagues simple bit-banged
2026-05-07 15:37:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] video.
