2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] To implement a red-only output while maintaining the existing timing structure, you need to adjust
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] your `pindirs` and `pins` logic. In a standard PAL DAC setup, color components are typically summed
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] or driven via specific pins.
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] Assuming your current hardware maps the "red" signal to a specific GPIO pin (e.g., GPIO 0 for Red,
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] GPIO 1 for Sync/Luma), you should modify the `active` loop to drive only the red pin while keeping
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] the luma/sync pin active as required.
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] Here is the refactored loop logic using a named function approach for clarity:
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] Refined `vidbit.pio` (Red Channel Focus)
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] ; vidbit.pio - Modified for Red-only active video
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] ; Assumes:
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] ; Pin 0: Red Video Data
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] ; Pin 1: Sync/Luma (Shared)
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] .program vidbit_red
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] ; ... (previous vsync logic remains the same) ...
2026-05-07 15:56:54 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] line:
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	pins, 0         ; HSYNC Low
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	pindirs, 3      ; Drive both pins
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	y, 26
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] hsync:
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	jmp	y--,hsync [28]
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	pindirs, 2      ; Back porch: Release Red (Pin 0), keep Sync (Pin 1)
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	pins, 2         ; Set Sync/Luma to pedestal
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	irq	set 4           ; Trigger Chroma SM
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	y, 29
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] backporch:
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	jmp	y--,backporch [31]
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	; Active Video: Drive only Red (Pin 0)
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	; We set pindirs to 1 (01 binary) so Pin 0 is driven, Pin 1 is high-z
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	mov	y, isr
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] active:
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	out	pins, 1 [8]     ; Output Red data to Pin 0
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	jmp	y--,active
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	; Front porch: Release all
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	pindirs, 0
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	set	y, 7
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] frontporch:
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	jmp	y--,frontporch [31]
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	jmp	x--,line [7]
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] .wrap
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
