2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] Key Considerations for the Red Output:
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  Pin Masking: By setting `pindirs` to `1` (binary `01`) during the `active` phase, you
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] ensure that only the Red bit is being pushed to the DAC. If your hardware uses a different pin for
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] Red, adjust the `out pins, 1` instruction or use `out pindirs, 2` to shift the bitmask.
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  DAC Bias: Ensure your reconstruction filter is biased to handle the Red signal
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] specifically. If you are using a 2-pin DAC for a single channel, you may need to adjust the
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] resistor values (the 100R/330R ladder) to match the voltage swing required for the Red video level
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] (typically 0.7V peak-to-peak).
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  Synchronization: Since you are using `irq 4` to trigger the `chroma` state machine,
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] ensure the `chroma` SM is configured to look for the same IRQ. If you are drawing only red,
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] the `chroma` SM should ideally be idle or outputting a black-level burst to maintain PAL standards.
2026-05-07 15:56:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
