2026-05-07 15:57:41 [gemini-3.1-lite] To send data to the `vidbit` state machine, you need to populate the FIFO with the structure the
2026-05-07 15:57:41 [gemini-3.1-lite] PIO expects (the sequence of line/pixel counts and the bitmap data).
2026-05-07 15:57:41 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:57:41 [gemini-3.1-lite] Since you are targeting "Red" output, you should prepare a buffer where each byte represents the
2026-05-07 15:57:41 [gemini-3.1-lite] pixel intensity (or bit-state) for your red channel. Here is a professional way to structure the
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] C++ data preparation using a helper function.
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] C++ Data Preparation
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
