2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] Implementation Notes:
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  DMA Integration (Recommended):
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite]     Because you are driving video, the CPU will likely be too slow to feed the FIFO manually
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] line-by-line. Use a DMA channel to transfer the buffer to the PIO `TX` register.
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Set the DMA `TREQ` to the PIO `DREQ` for the specific state machine.
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Use a circular buffer if you are generating dynamic content.
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  Bit Packing:
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite]     The PIO `out pins, 1` instruction consumes 1 bit per cycle. If you are sending `uint32_t` from
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] C++, the PIO will process 32 pixels per word. Make sure your C++ logic packs the "Red" bits into
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] this 32-bit format correctly. If your image is 8-bit color, you will need a conversion function to
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] threshold that into a 1-bit Red signal.
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  Buffer Alignment:
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite]     Ensure your `buffer` is large enough to contain the control words (the first 4 indices) plus
2026-05-07 15:57:42 [gemini-3.1-lite] the total number of pixels divided by 32.
2026-05-07 15:57:43 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 15:57:43 [gemini-3.1-lite] 4.  Synchronization:
2026-05-07 15:57:43 [gemini-3.1-lite]     Since you have `irq 4` in your PIO code, your C++ code should ideally have an interrupt handler
2026-05-07 15:57:43 [gemini-3.1-lite] or a polling loop that resets the DMA pointers at the start of every frame (triggered by the PIO
2026-05-07 15:57:43 [gemini-3.1-lite] IRQ) to ensure the video data stays aligned with the CRT/monitor scanlines.
2026-05-07 15:57:43 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
