2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] Your C++ implementation is now architecturally complete. You have successfully decoupled the
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] Luma/Sync path on `pio0` from the Chroma path on `pio1`, and you are utilizing DMA to feed both.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] To ensure this actually produces a valid PAL color image on your hardware, here is your final
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] "Pre-Flight" checklist:
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1. The "Color Burst" Timing
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] In `initChroma()`, you have `if(i < 3)`. Since your `chroma` SM is clocked at 4x f_sc, each word
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] you send is 16 steps (4 subcarrier cycles). Sending 3 words gives you exactly 12 cycles of the
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] color burst. This is perfect for a PAL signal, as it provides enough time for the TV’s
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] phase-locked loop (PLL) to lock onto the burst frequency and phase.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2. The Burst Amplitude
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] Ensure that your `burst` constant (`0x23102310`) results in a 300mV peak-to-peak signal at the
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] output. If the colors are "washed out" or the TV doesn't switch to color mode, this is almost
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] always due to the burst amplitude being too low.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3. The Phase Inversion (The "PAL" part)
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] You are currently using `0x55555555` and `0xCCCCCCCC` for the active video. These are static
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] patterns.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] • To get color: You need to replace these with a sequence that represents the subcarrier
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] sine wave.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] • To get "Red": You must shift the phase of that sine wave by ~104°.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] • The Inversion: In your `initChroma` function, you should eventually replace the `0x55...`
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] and `0xCC...` with the phase-inverted sine wave logic I provided earlier. If you don't invert the
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] phase on `oddRed`, you will likely get "Hanover Bars" (horizontal bands of color error) because the
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] TV expects the V-axis to flip every line.
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 4. A Note on `piosmset_enabled`
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] In your `main` loop, you have:
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] if(!started){
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite]     vid_start(pio0,VideoStateMachine);
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite]     started=true;
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] You should also enable the `chroma` SM here:
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] if(!started){
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite]     vid_start(pio0, VideoStateMachine);
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite]     pio_sm_set_enabled(pio1, ChromaStateMachine, true); // Add this
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite]     started=true;
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-05-07 16:20:52 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] This ensures that the Chroma SM starts waiting for the `irq 4` trigger at the exact same moment the
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] video timing begins.
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] Final Debugging Advice
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] • If the screen is stable but black and white: The TV is not detecting the burst. Check
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] your scope on the `CHROMA` pins during the back porch.
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] • If you see rolling diagonal lines: Your subcarrier frequency is slightly off. Since you
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] are using a 166.5MHz system clock, your `clkdiv` in the PIO config must be precisely calculated to
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] hit 17.734475 MHz. If the color is "crawling," adjust your PIO `clkdiv` slightly.
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] • If you see color but it's the wrong hue: You need to adjust the phase shift in your
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] sine-wave generation loop.
2026-05-07 16:20:53 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
