2026-05-07 18:09:29 [nitro@ryzen5] can we calc when after back porch should colorburst happen?
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] To calculate the precise timing for the color burst, we must align it with the PAL standard
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] specifications relative to the Back Porch (the period immediately following the H-sync
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] pulse).
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] PAL Timing Constants
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • System Clock (f_sys): 166.5 MHz
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Target Subcarrier (f_sc): 4.43361875 MHz
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • PIO Frequency: 4 × f_sc = 17.734475 MHz
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Cycles per Line: 10656 (at 166.5 MHz)
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • H-Sync Duration: \approx 4.7 µs (\approx 786 cycles)
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Back Porch Duration: \approx 5.79 µs (\approx 964 cycles)
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] The Burst Timing
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] According to ITU-R BT.470, the Color Burst starts shortly after the trailing edge of the
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] H-sync pulse.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  Start Delay: The burst starts 0.9 µs to 1.1 µs after the trailing edge of the
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] sync pulse.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  Duration: It consists of 10 ± 1 cycles of the color subcarrier.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] Calculation for your PIO
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] Since your `vidbit.pio` handles the line timing, we define the start of the burst relative to the
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] start of the Back Porch:
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Conversion: At 166.5 MHz, 1.0\text µs \approx 166.5 cycles.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • PIO Alignment: Your PIO runs at 17.734475 MHz. In the PIO time domain:
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   1.0\text µs × 17.734475\text MHz \approx \mathbf17.7 \text cycles.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] Implementation Strategy
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] You should trigger the `chroma` PIO state machine (which generates the burst) by using an `irq`
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] signal from the `vidbit` PIO.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  In `vidbit.pio`:
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     Place an `irq set 4` instruction exactly 18 cycles into the Back Porch sequence.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     ; Inside backporch section
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     set	pins, 1
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     nop [16]        ; Wait ~1.0us
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     irq set 4       ; Trigger Chroma PIO
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     set y, 28       ; Remaining back porch
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     ...
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  In `chroma.pio`:
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite]     The `wait 1 irq 4` instruction at the start of your `chroma` program will now catch this
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] trigger. Since the burst itself is 10 cycles long, and your `chroma` program outputs 4 bits per
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] subcarrier cycle, you need to output 40 bits (or 10 words if your PIO logic consumes 4 bits
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] per loop) to complete the burst.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] Refined Logic
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • The "Gap": The burst must end at least 0.5 µs before the start of the active video line.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Calculation: 10 cycles of 4.43 MHz is \approx 2.25 µs.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Total timing: 1.0 µs (gap) + 2.25 µs (burst) = 3.25 µs.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Since your Back Porch is 5.79 µs, you have plenty of room. Setting the `irq` at the ~1 µs mark is
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] mathematically safe and compliant with the PAL specification.
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Recommendation:* If you see the burst "bleeding" into the active video area, decrease the
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] `nop` count in the `vidbit` PIO. If the colors are washed out, verify your `chroma` PIO `clkdiv` is
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] correctly hitting the subcarrier frequency so that the 10 cycles fit within the expected time
2026-05-07 18:09:35 [gemini-3.1-lite] window.
2026-05-07 18:09:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Your implementation of the `irq` trigger is positioned well. Let's verify the timing math to ensure
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] the burst sits correctly within the back porch.
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Timing Verification (166.5 MHz)
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  The Trigger point:
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `set pins, 1` (1 cycle)
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `nop [16]` (17 cycles)
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `irq set 4` (1 cycle)
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Total: 19 cycles from the start of the back porch.
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   19 / 166.5 \text MHz \approx \mathbf0.114 \text µs.
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  The PAL Specification:
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Standard PAL burst start is typically 0.9 µs to 1.1 µs after the trailing edge of
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] H-sync.
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Your current trigger is at 0.114 µs. This is likely too early and may cause
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] the burst to overlap with the H-sync trailing edge or the very start of the back porch, which can
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] confuse TV sync separators.
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Recommended Adjustment
2026-05-07 18:11:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] To hit the 1.0 µs target, you need approximately 166 cycles.
