2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] A Note on `chroma.pio` Execution
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] Your `chroma.pio` starts with `wait 1 irq 4`. When the `vidbit` PIO triggers the IRQ, the `chroma`
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] PIO will immediately begin its execution.
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Instruction Latency: `wait` takes 1 cycle, and the subsequent `out` takes 1 cycle. This
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] is negligible.
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Burst Duration: If you want 10 cycles of burst, and your `chroma.pio` loop outputs 4 bits
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] (1 cycle) per iteration, you need to output 10 words (assuming 1 subcarrier cycle per word
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] output).
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Safety: Ensure the `chroma` PIO finishes its burst before the `active` section in
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] `vidbit.pio` begins.
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Burst end = (Start Delay) + (Burst Duration)
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Burst end = 1.0 µs + 2.25 µs = 3.25 µs.
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Your back porch is 5.79 µs. You have ~2.5 µs of "quiet" time before the active video
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] starts. This is perfect for preventing color subcarrier interference with the luminance signal.
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] One structural suggestion
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] In `vidbit.pio`, you are using `set pins, 1` to define the back porch level. If your hardware
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] reconstruction filter relies on the DAC being in a specific state (e.g., blanking level) during the
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] back porch, ensure that `set pins, 1` corresponds exactly to that voltage level. If the color burst
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] is modulated on top of this, the `chroma` PIO output should be mixed accordingly.
2026-05-07 18:11:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
