2026-05-07 18:13:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     In your `initChroma` function, you are correctly generating the `oddRed` and `evenRed` buffers.
2026-05-07 18:13:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Since you are using the same `burst` constant for the first three words, ensure these match the
2026-05-07 18:13:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] duration of the 10-cycle burst.
2026-05-07 18:13:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]        Note*: If you find the color burst is too long or short, you can adjust the
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] `colorWords` DMA count in `vid_field`.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  PIO IRQ Latency:
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     When `vidbit` triggers `irq 4`, the `chroma` PIO executes its `wait 1 irq 4` instruction. There
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] is a 1-cycle latency before the `chroma` PIO begins its `out` sequence. This is effectively
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] "jitter-free" because both state machines are clocked by the same system clock.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  Output Pin Conflict:
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     You are using `VIDPIN` (22) for Luminance and `CHROMA100PIN` (20) / `CHROMA330_PIN`
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] (21) for Chroma.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]        Hardware Mixing: Your resistor network (120Ω/150Ω/330Ω/100Ω) is designed to sum
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] these signals. Ensure that when `chroma` is not* sending a burst, the pins are driven to a
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] state that does not pull the video signal out of the blanking level.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   Recommendation: In `chroma.pio`, ensure the `set` or `out` instructions during
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] non-burst times drive the chroma pins to a "neutral" state (typically high impedance or ground,
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] depending on your filter design). Your `chroma.pio` should ideally include a `set pins, 0` or
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] similar idle state after the burst loop finishes.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 4.  DMA Synchronization:
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     You are using `dmachannelisbusy` to trigger `vidfield`. This is excellent for
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] keeping the frame buffers in sync with the line count. One minor suggestion: since you are using
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] `pio1` for Chroma and `pio0` for Video, if you encounter "color tearing" (where the color is
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] slightly shifted horizontally relative to the luminance), it is likely due to the DMA start latency
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] between the two state machines.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]        Fix*: If this occurs, you can use the same `irq 4` trigger to start both the `video`
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] DMA and the `chroma` DMA simultaneously by linking them to the same PIO IRQ flag if necessary.
2026-05-07 18:13:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
