2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] PAL Compliance
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] This is perfect. The ITU-R BT.470 standard specifies that the color burst should start
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 0.9 µs to 1.1 µs after the trailing edge of the H-sync pulse. Your implementation lands at
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 0.914 µs, placing the start of the burst exactly at the beginning of the allowed tolerance
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] window.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] Observations on your Implementation
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • DMA Pacing: By using `chromadmainit` with `colorWords` (120) and a `dreq` to
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] `pio1`, you are ensuring that the subcarrier stream is perfectly phase-locked to the line timing.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Padding as "Blanking": Using `0` as the padding word is the correct approach. Since your
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] reconstruction filter is likely AC-coupled or referenced to the blanking level, sending `0` (which
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] presumably maps to the lowest DAC voltage on those pins) effectively keeps the chroma output at the
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] "no-color" level until the burst begins.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • V-Flip: Your `initChroma` loop correctly handles the PAL V-flip by swapping phase 1 and 2
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] for odd lines. This will ensure that the color subcarrier phase is correctly inverted every other
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] line, which is mandatory for PAL compatibility.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] Minor Recommendation
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] If you find that the color is slightly "shifted" horizontally, it is because the luminance
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] (`vidbit`) and chrominance (`chroma`) are generated by two different PIO state machines.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • If you see "color fringing" on the left edge of objects, it means the color subcarrier is
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] arriving slightly late relative to the luminance.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] • You can "fine-tune" this by shifting the `irq` trigger in `vidbit.pio` by a few `nop`
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] instructions or by adding/removing a padding word in the `initChroma` buffer.
2026-05-07 18:15:30 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
