2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] More importantly, even when you re-enable `CHROMA`, there is a likely structural issue:
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] Chroma is waiting on an IRQ from the wrong PIO block
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] `vidbit.pio` runs on PIO0:
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] pass &= vid_init(pio0, VideoStateMachine);
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] and it does:
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] irq	set 4
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] But chroma is initialised on PIO1:
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] pass &= chroma_init(pio1, ChromaStateMachine);
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] chroma_dma_init(pio1, ChromaStateMachine);
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] and `chroma.pio` waits for:
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] wait	1 irq 4
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] PIO IRQ flags are local to each PIO block. A state machine on `pio1` will not see `irq set 4` from
2026-05-08 10:26:07 [gpt-5.5-2026] `pio0`. So if chroma is enabled as-is, the chroma SM should sit waiting forever, or at least never
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] line-sync from the video SM.
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] That is probably the main reason you were still seeing monochrome before.
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] Suggested test
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] Keep video on `pio0`, but move chroma to another state machine on the same PIO, for
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] example:
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] - video: `pio0`, SM0
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] - teletext: `pio0`, SM1 if enabled
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] - chroma: `pio0`, SM2 or SM3
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] Then leave I2S on `pio1`.
2026-05-08 10:26:08 [gpt-5.5-2026] 
