2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • fs.cpp*
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The comment says "1MB" but `blockcount = 512` at 4KB blocks is actually 2MB. One of those needs
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] correcting. Also `lfsformat` is called unconditionally in `lfs_test` — fine as a scratch test
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] but would wipe existing data on every call in production use.
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The read/write addressing split is correctly handled — reads use the XIP-mapped absolute address,
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] writes and erases use the raw `FLASHTARGETOFFSET` as the SDK requires. That's easy to get
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] wrong.
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • Flash operations during video*
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] `saveanddisable_interrupts` is used correctly, and since the video DMA feeds directly from
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] RAM frame buffers into PIO, XIP suspension during flash writes won't disturb the signal. That's a
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] fortunate consequence of the RAM-based frame buffer design.
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • i2s.cpp*
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The LFSR with a hold counter is a neat way to produce textured noise rather than pure white. The
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] `0xdeadbeef` seed is fine. `fuzz` and `tick` as file-scope globals work here but would be worth
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] encapsulating if the audio side grows.
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • pal576i.cpp*
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The equalizing and broad sync pulse structure looks correct for PAL 625-line interlaced, with the
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] half-line `S0,S1` handoff between fields handled properly.
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • monobit.cpp*
2026-05-08 13:32:59 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The `c64_rgb` array is defined but appears unused currently — presumably reserved for chroma work.
