2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] These are new to me — quite a substantial project. A few observations:
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • PIO Design*
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The `out pindirs, 1` approach for pixel output is elegant — using pin direction to toggle between
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] driven-low (sync/black) and high-impedance (pulled high via resistor ladder = white) rather than
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] toggling the pin value itself. Clean way to get two video levels from one pin.
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • Resistor Network*
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The 120Ω/150Ω/75Ω network in the header comment is a tidy approach to composite mono. The chroma
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] additions (100Ω/330Ω) suggest colour work is in progress rather than complete.
2026-05-09 21:40:02 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • WST Teletext*
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] The Hamming 8/4 encoding and clock run-in (0x55, 0x55, 0x27) look correct for the standard. One
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] thing worth verifying is the byte timing relationship between the WST DMA and the video DMA —
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] teletext packets need to land in lines 7–22 precisely.
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • Filesystem*
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] `FSBASEADDRESS` is referenced in `fs.cpp` but not defined in the shared files — presumably
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] lives in CMakeLists or a board config. Worth confirming the `lfsRead` uses it as an absolute XIP
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] address while `lfsProg`/`lfsErase` correctly convert to a flash offset.
2026-05-09 21:40:03 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
