2026-05-09 21:48:19 [nitro@ryzen5] hello are you ok claude?
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] Hello, yes fine thanks for asking.
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] On the WST timing — the core issue is that the `irq set 0` fires at the start of the back porch,
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] and the WST PIO presumably waits on that IRQ then delays before outputting data. When you shift the
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] porch counts, two things change:
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] 
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] • Total line length* — if the porch adjustments don't net to zero, the line is no longer
2026-05-09 21:49:56 [claude-sonnet-4-6] exactly 10656 cycles, which will cause cumulative drift across fields.
