2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] The IRQ position (at the start of the back porch) is correct for WST teletext if the WST delay
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] matches the back porch length. Your current `wst.pio` sets `y=28` and delays for 957 cycles, which
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] exactly equals the back porch duration (28 loop iterations × 33 cycles + 33 for the last
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] fall-through ≈ 957). So the first teletext bit should align with the start of active video.
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] That part is fine.
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] However, there is a critical timing error in `vidbit.pio` itself. I have recalculated the actual
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] line cycles from your code:
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] ╭────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────╮
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  Section                   │  Calculated cycles  │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] ├────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  Hsync setup + loop        │  813                │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  Back porch setup + loop   │  961                │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  Active video              │  9504               │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  Front porch setup + loop  │  265                │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  Wrap `jmp x--,line [12]`  │  13                 │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] │  **Total**                 │  **11556**          │
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] ╰────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────╯
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] The intended total is 10656 cycles (64 µs at 166.5 MHz). Your line is ~900 cycles too long,
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] which will:
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] - Make the line duration ~69.4 µs instead of 64 µs → cumulative field length error
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] - Shift the WST transmission later relative to the next sync, potentially causing decoder dropout
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] - Cause the active pixel count to exceed the declared 864, because the `mov y,isr` loads a counter
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] of 863 but the loop runs 864 iterations (y=863 down to 0). Each iteration takes 11 cycles (9 for
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] `out [8]` + 2 for taken `jmp`), but the comment assumes 10 cycles. The mismatch comes from the
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] `jmp` costing 2 cycles when taken, not 1.
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] • Recommended fix:*
2026-05-09 23:00:58 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] Adjust the active pixel loop to bring the total to 10656. For example, reduce the number of delay
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] slots in the `out` instruction or change the pixel counter. The simplest patch:
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] active:
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4]     out pindirs, 1 [7]      ; was [8] → 8 cycles per pixel
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4]     jmp y--, active
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] This changes each pixel from 11 to 10 cycles (8 + 2). Then:
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] - 864 pixels × 10 = 8640 cycles
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] - Plus `mov y,isr` (1) and last non-taken jmp (1) = 8642 cycles (matches the comment).
2026-05-09 23:00:59 [deepseek-v4] 
