2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for sharing these PIO programs. They form a coherent set for a video generation system on
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] a Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (RP2350), likely for generating PAL 576i composite video with chroma, plus
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] audio (I2S/SPDIF), PS/2, IR, and teletext.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] Key observations:
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] - System clock 166.5 MHz is unusual (non-standard for RP2350) but chosen to make PAL
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] subcarrier (4.43361875 MHz) exact with a PIO divider of 9.3885. This level of precision suggests
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] careful derivation.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] - The `chroma.pio` uses a 4‑cycle per bit loop to generate two 90° phase increments per FIFO byte,
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] producing 8‑bit color subcarrier samples. Running at 17.734 MHz (4× f_sc) this yields exactly 2
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] subcarrier cycles per byte.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] - `pixelpump.pio` and `vidbit.pio` coordinate line timing: `vidbit` generates HSYNC, back porch,
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] active video (864 pixels = 27 words), and front porch. `pixelpump` forwards a 27‑word FIFO pipeline
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] on each IRQ0.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] - The `onebit.pio` and `threepin.pio` decouple pixel data into bit‑serial output – `onebit` selects
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] between two 32‑bit waveforms based on a feedback pin, while `threepin` drives 3 tristate pins from
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] a 30‑bit per word payload (10 groups of 3 bits, plus 2 skipped bits for alpha – clever).
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] - `hilo32.pio` is a precise pulse‑width measurer (32‑bit elapsed cycles), fitting well for edge
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] timing of IR (RC5) or PS/2.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] - The `wst.pio` teletext generator outputs only the data burst (0 or 384 bits) triggered by IRQ0,
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] similar to the active video timing.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] The overall architecture is FIFO‑pipelined (pixelpump → onebit → threepin) with each stage
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] triggered by IRQs or pin feedback, achieving deterministic video timing without CPU intervention
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] after setup.
2026-05-11 12:49:01 [deepseek-v4] 
