2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Update the DMA Initialization
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] Replace your `colorpumpdmainit` function with this. Notice how we use
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] `channelconfigsetring(&ctrlc, true, 3);`. This applies an 8-byte ring to the
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] write address, meaning it writes to `0x38`, then `0x3C`, and wraps perfectly back to `0x38`
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] for the next line!
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] void colorpump_dma_init(PIO pio, int sm) {
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Initialize the control blocks for the field
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for (int i = 0; i < progressiveLines; i++) {
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		colorpump_ctrl_blocks[i * 2] = colorpumpStride;            // Word 1: trans_count
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		colorpump_ctrl_blocks[i * 2 + 1] = (uint32_t)colorTest;    // Word 2: read_addr
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	}
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	colorpump_dma_chan = dma_claim_unused_channel(true);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	colorpump_ctrl_chan = dma_claim_unused_channel(true);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// --- 1. Control Channel Setup ---
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	dma_channel_config ctrl_c = dma_channel_get_default_config(colorpump_ctrl_chan);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_transfer_data_size(&ctrl_c, DMA_SIZE_32);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_read_increment(&ctrl_c, true);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_write_increment(&ctrl_c, true);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// MAGIC: 8-byte write ring. Forces writes to wrap between TRANS_COUNT and READ_ADDR_TRIG
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_ring(&ctrl_c, true, 3);
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	dma_channel_configure(
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		colorpump_ctrl_chan,
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		&ctrl_c,
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		&dma_hw->ch[colorpump_dma_chan].al3_transfer_count, // Write to Data channel's Alias 3
2026-05-12 16:27:35 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		colorpump_ctrl_blocks,                              // Read from our control blocks
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		0,                                                  // Don't start yet
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		false
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	);
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// --- 2. Data Channel Setup ---
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	dma_channel_config c = dma_channel_get_default_config(colorpump_dma_chan);
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_transfer_data_size(&c, DMA_SIZE_32);
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_read_increment(&c, true);
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_write_increment(&c, false);
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_dreq(&c, pio_get_dreq(pio, sm, true));
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Chain to the control channel when 108 words are finished
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	channel_config_set_chain_to(&c, colorpump_ctrl_chan);
2026-05-12 16:27:36 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
