2026-05-13 08:19:44 [gemini-3.1-pro] To do this, you generally first need to parse the JSON string into a native data structure, such as
2026-05-13 08:19:44 [gemini-3.1-pro] an object or a dictionary, depending on the programming language you are using. Once parsed, most
2026-05-13 08:19:44 [gemini-3.1-pro] languages provide built-in methods to retrieve a collection of those keys, allowing you to easily
2026-05-13 08:19:44 [gemini-3.1-pro] check the total count or length of that collection.
