2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] straightforward.
2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] You can achieve this by using the built-in `Object.keys()` method. This method takes your
2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] JavaScript object as an argument and returns an array containing all of the object's enumerable
2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] property names (the keys). Once you have that array, you can simply check its `length` property to
2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] get the total count of the keys.
2026-05-13 08:20:04 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
