2026-05-13 09:02:11 [nitro@ryzen5] there are some issues with colorpump, i think main one is irq is stuck
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] It sounds like you are running into a classic hardware boundary trap with the PIO. Based on the
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] architecture and code provided, there are a few interconnected reasons why your `colorpump` IRQ is
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] getting stuck.
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is a breakdown of what is likely happening and how to address it:
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 1. Cross-PIO IRQ Visibility*
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] In `vidbit.cpp`, your main video generator (`vidbit`) is initialized on `pio0`, while `colorpump`
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] is initialized on `pio1`.
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] On the RP2350 (and RP2040), the 8 internal state machine IRQ flags are strictly local to each PIO
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] block. State machines on `pio1` cannot see or wait on IRQ flags set by state machines on `pio0`. If
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] your main video timing on `pio0` is setting IRQ 5 to trigger the line pump, `colorpump` on `pio1`
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] will never see it go high, causing it to stall indefinitely at the `wait` instruction.
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] To fix this, you will need to move `colorpump` to `pio0` so they share the same IRQ flag pool.
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 2. State Machine ID Conflict*
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] If you move `colorpump` to `pio0`, you will need to assign it a free state machine index.
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] Currently, your state machine IDs are defined as:
2026-05-13 09:03:15 [gemini-3.1-pro] • `VideoStateMachine = 0`
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • `TeletextStateMachine = 1`
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • `ColorPumpStateMachine = 1`
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • `ChromaStateMachine = 1`
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] Notice that `ColorPumpStateMachine` and `ChromaStateMachine` share the same ID (`1`). While
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] `CHROMA` is currently commented out, this will cause a collision if both are ever enabled.
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] Additionally, if you move `colorpump` to `pio0`, it will collide with `TeletextStateMachine`.
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] I recommend reassigning `ColorPumpStateMachine` to `2` and updating your `main()` function to
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] initialize it on `pio0` instead of `pio1`.
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 3. Clearing the IRQ Flag*
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] In your `colorpump.pio` file, the synchronization instruction is written as:
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] `wait 1 irq 5`
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] This tells the state machine to wait until the flag is high, but it does not clear the
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] flag. Unless your main `vidbit` state machine is manually clearing IRQ 5 immediately after setting
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] it, `colorpump` will blast right through the `wait` instruction on all subsequent lines and lose
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] synchronization.
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] You can instruct the PIO to automatically clear the flag once the wait condition is met by
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] appending the `clear` modifier to the instruction in your PIO assembly:
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] `wait 1 irq 5 clear`
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-13 09:03:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
