2026-05-13 09:12:57 [nitro@ryzen5] txfifo is not supported for reads
2026-05-13 09:12:59 [nitro@ryzen5] 	mov	osr, rxfifo[y]
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] You are absolutely right, and I apologize for the oversight. The RP2350 PIO introduced the ability
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] to index the RX FIFO (`rxfifo[y]`), but it does not support indexed reads from the TX FIFO.
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because `piosmput_blocking` writes directly to the TX FIFO, the data never makes it into
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] the RX FIFO where your `colorfifo` state machine is attempting to read it, leaving the arrays full
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] of zeroes.
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] To resolve this, we need to move the data from the TX FIFO into the RX FIFO during the
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] initialization phase. We can achieve this by briefly instructing the state machine to pull the word
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] from the TX FIFO, move it to the ISR, and push it into the RX FIFO.
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is a reusable helper function you can add to `vidbit.cpp` to handle this:
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] void preload_rxfifo(PIO pio, int sm, uint32_t data) {
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_put_blocking(pio, sm, data);
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_exec(pio, sm, pio_encode_pull(false, false));
2026-05-13 09:13:33 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_exec(pio, sm, pio_encode_mov(pio_isr, pio_osr));
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_exec(pio, sm, pio_encode_push(false, false));
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] You can then update the `colorfifo` initialization loop in `colorpumpinit` to use this function
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] instead of `piosmputblocking`:
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for(int fifo = 0; fifo < 4; fifo++) {
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		pio_sm_config config7 = colorfifo_program_get_default_config(offset7);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		sm_config_set_in_pins(&config7, COLOR_I0);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		// colorfifo sets/outs to Y_PIN, PB_PIN, PR_PIN (3 pins)
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		sm_config_set_out_pins(&config7, Y_PIN, 3);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		sm_config_set_set_pins(&config7, Y_PIN, 3);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		sm_config_set_jmp_pin(&config7, PUMP0_ENABLE + fifo);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		pio_sm_init(pio2, fifo, offset7, &config7);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			preload_rxfifo(pio2, fifo, color_trains[color_index]);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			color_index++;
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		}
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		pio_sm_set_enabled(pio2, fifo, true);
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	}
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] Combined with enabling `autopull` on `colorpump` and ensuring `colorpump` is running on `pio0` to
2026-05-13 09:13:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] share the IRQ pool, this will complete the data path and populate your color trains correctly.
