2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] You can do it without adding a cycle to the active 10-cycle train.
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] Best trick: move the sanitize work into the stall loop (only runs while disabled), then
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] reuse `y` for the live cycle.
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] So instead of reading pins after release, pre-read while stalled:
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] - in stall: keep sampling index into `y`
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] - when gate opens: immediately use `rxfifo[y]`
2026-05-13 09:33:20 [gpt-5.3-codex] - then output your 6×`out pindirs,3` + housekeeping unchanged
