2026-05-14 09:39:46 [nitro@ryzen5] how do i do this in ts
2026-05-14 09:39:47 [nitro@ryzen5] class share{	id:string,	path:string,	name:string}
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] In TypeScript, to create an array of a specific type, you first define the type (using an
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] interface, type alias, or class), then declare the array using the type followed by `[]` or
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] `Array<Type>`.
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] For the structure you provided (which looks like an object with properties `id`, `path`, `name`),
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] you can define it as:
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] // Using an interface (most common for data objects)
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] interface Share {
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   id: string;
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   path: string;
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   name: string;
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] // Or using a type alias
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] type Share = {
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   id: string;
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   path: string;
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   name: string;
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] };
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] // Then declare an array of that type
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] let sharedfiles: Share[] = [];       // Preferred
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] // or
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] let sharedfiles: Array<Share> = [];  // Equivalent
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] If you prefer a class (e.g., to include methods), you can define:
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] class Share {
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   constructor(
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]     public id: string,
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]     public path: string,
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]     public name: string
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4]   ) {}
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] let sharedfiles: Share[] = [];
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 09:39:52 [deepseek-v4] Now `sharedfiles` is typed as an array of `Share` objects, giving you full IntelliSense and type
2026-05-14 09:39:52 [deepseek-v4] safety.
