2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] assume you mean to use `side‑set` or `out` for FIFO control? Actually, PIO assembler doesn't have a
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] `.fifo` directive. You probably intended `.side_set 1` or something else. Please clarify the
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] intended pin mapping and side‑set usage.
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] - `mov y, pins` reads the current GPIO pins. Which pins? The `pins` register reflects the actual
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] pin levels. If colour indices come from `colorpump` via dedicated GPIO pairs, this works. However,
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] the timing of reading `pins` relative to the trigger needs to be tight to avoid races.
