2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] Signal Chain (`vidpump.md`)
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] - `pixelpump` → `onebit` → `threepin` is a three‑stage pipeline. The inter‑state machine
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] synchronisation via `irq` (clear/set) is good. However, note that `threepin` uses `jmp y--, train`
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] which loops for the full line pixel count. The `pull block` at the start of `threepin` waits for a
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] pixel count from the previous stage. Ensure the FIFO depth and back‑pressure are adequate to avoid
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] stalls.
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] - In `onebit`, you use `out pins, 1` to read pixel data from OSR. But the `pins` output is used as
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] feedback via a loopback pin (GP46). That loopback pin then drives `jmp pin` to select between two
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] waveform tables. This is clever, but note that `out pins, 1` changes the output
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] immediately; the loopback pin will reflect that value on the next clock cycle. Ensure the
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] pipeline timing accounts for one cycle delay, otherwise the wrong waveform may be selected for the
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] current pixel.
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] - The two waveform tables (`y` and `x`) are loaded once per line? Actually `onebit` loads them
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] before the pixel loop, so they remain constant for the whole line. This is fine for a monochrome or
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] fixed‑palette display, but for per‑pixel colour the waveform would need to change per pixel. Your
2026-05-14 11:15:14 [deepseek-v4] `colorpump`+`colorfifo` approach is separate – does that replace `onebit`? The description says
2026-05-14 11:15:15 [deepseek-v4] "pixelpump → onebit → threepin" for 1‑bit video, while `colorpump` seems to be for a fully coloured
2026-05-14 11:15:15 [deepseek-v4] component signal. You may have two distinct modes; please clarify.
