2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] Suggested integration
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] Given you have two colour strategies, I think you could unify them:
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] - Option A (component output): Use the `pixelpump/onebit/threepin` chain for three 1‑bit
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] colour channels (R, G, B) – i.e., each channel gets its own `onebit` and `threepin`. This gives
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 8‑colour analogue video via resistor DACs. Or extend to multiple bits per channel using additional
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] state machines.
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] - Option B (indexed palette): Stick with `colorpump/colorfifo` for a fixed palette of 4
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] colours, each with full flexibility of waveform shape. This is simpler for teletext or retro
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] graphics.
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] • Potential improvements*:
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 1. Avoid multiple FIFO passes: Instead of three state machines, you could combine
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] `pixelpump` and `onebit` into one state machine that loads two patterns and outputs directly to
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] pins. But that loses modularity.
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 2. Check pin direction timing: Every `out pindirs, 3` updates the pin direction (pin as
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] output). You should ensure that between lines the pins are set to input (or pulled low) to prevent
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] glitches during H‑sync.
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 3. Adjust `threepin` cycle count: You have 7 `out pindirs` but earlier you wrote “10 pixel
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] cycles” – the comment in `colorfifo.pio` also says “6 cycles + 4 housekeeping”. Align these: if a
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] pixel is 10 cycles, you need 10 `out pindirs` grouped, not 7. The current `threepin` does 7 + 1
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] (set) + 11 dummy = 19? Actually 7×3=21 bits, then `set pindirs,0` takes a cycle, then `out null,11`
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] consumes 11 cycles? But `out null` doesn’t advance the program counter in the same way – check PIO
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] manual: `out null` does consume a cycle but does not change any output. So total = 7+1+1+1+11=21
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] cycles? This is inconsistent with 10‑cycle pixel. You probably want exactly 10 cycles per pixel: 6
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] waveform groups + 1 zero group + 3 no‑op (or `set pindirs,0` and two `nop`). The comment in
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] `colorfifo.pio` says “6 cycles + 4 housekeeping” – that’s 10 cycles total. Revise `threepin`
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] accordingly.
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 12:51:23 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
