2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] Reviewing the shared files for the RP2350 PAL video system. Notable observations:
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] Architecture Overview
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] • System Clock:* 166.5 MHz, PAL 576i interlaced video (625 lines @ 25Hz)
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Line Timing:* 64µs per line = 10,656 cycles @ 166.5MHz = 10 cycles/pixel
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] • PIO State Machines:*
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] - SM0: `vidbit.pio` - Main PAL sync/video waveform
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] - SM1: `greyline.pio` - Greyscale luma output (GP18)
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] - SM1: `chroma.pio` - PAL color burst (2-pin DAC)
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] - SM2: `wst.pio` - World System Teletext data insertion
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] - SM2: `i2s.pio` - Audio I2S interface (48kHz stereo)
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] - SM3: `ps2.pio` - PS/2 keyboard input
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] Interesting Design Patterns
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:19:33 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 1. Dual-field Interlace*
