2026-05-15 13:30:40 [claude-haiku-4-5] Chapter 11: PIO (Programmable Input/Output)
2026-05-15 13:30:40 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.1 Overview
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] RP2350 contains 3 identical PIO blocks. Each PIO block has:
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - 4 state machines
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Dedicated connections to bus fabric, GPIO, and interrupt controller
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Shared 32-instruction memory (all 4 SMs read from same memory)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Each state machine includes:*
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Two 32-bit shift registers (ISR, OSR)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Two 32-bit scratch registers (X, Y)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - 4 × 32-bit TX/RX FIFOs (reconfigurable as 8×32 single direction)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Fractional clock divider (16-bit integer + 8-bit fractional)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Flexible GPIO mapping
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - DMA interface (up to 1 word/clock throughput)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - 8 IRQ flags (shareable across PIO blocks)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Silicon efficiency:* Each SM occupies roughly the same area as a standard serial
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] interface (SPI/I2C), but provides vastly more flexibility.
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Performance:* Can sustain 360 Mb/s (DPI output @ 48 MHz system clock).
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.1.1 Changes from RP2040 → RP2350
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] ╭───────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  Feature                  │  RP2350                   │  Use Case                                  │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] ├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **Version field**        │  DBG_CFGINFO.VERSION = 1  │  Runtime feature detection                 │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **GPIO base**            │  GPIOBASE register        │  Support >32 GPIOs per block               │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **Cross-PIO sync**       │  CTRL.NEXT/PREV_PIO_MASK  │  Sync state machines across blocks         │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **Input masking**        │  SM0_SHIFTCTRL.IN_COUNT   │  MOV x, PINS returns only needed bits      │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **All 8 IRQs exposed**   │  IRQ0_INTE, IRQ1_INTE     │  System-level interrupts from all flags    │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **Indexed RX FIFO GET**  │  `mov osr, rxfifo[y]`     │  Random-access lookup tables (v1 only)     │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **Indexed RX FIFO PUT**  │  `mov rxfifo[y], isr`     │  Random-access status registers (v1 only)  │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **PINDIRS in MOV**       │  `mov pindirs, x`         │  Bulk pin direction control                │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **MOV STATUS**           │  SM IRQ flags as source   │  Conditional jumps on IRQ state            │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **Cross-PIO IRQ**        │  `irq next/prev set n`    │  IRQ coordination across PIO blocks        │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] │  **WAIT JMPPIN offset**   │  `wait 1 jmppin +2`       │  Flexible branch pin selection             │
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] ╰───────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.2 Programmer's Model
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.2.1 PIO Programs
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - 9 instructions total: JMP, WAIT, IN, OUT, PUSH, PULL, MOV, IRQ, SET
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Assembly format: `.pio` text files → compiled by `pioasm` → C header constants
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Execution: 1 instruction per clock (unless stalled)
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Delays: 0-31 cycle inserts before next instruction
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Example: Square wave*
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] .program squarewave
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] set pindirs, 1      ; Set pin to output
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] again:
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5]     set pins, 1 [1] ; Drive high, delay 1 cycle
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5]     set pins, 0     ; Drive low
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5]     jmp again       ; Loop
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:41 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.2.2 Control Flow
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Program Counter (PC):*
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Increments by 1 each cycle (wraps at end of memory)
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - JMP instructions set PC explicitly
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - WAIT stalls without advancing PC
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Side-set executes even during stall
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Clock divider:* Scales state machine speed by fractional factor (1 to 65536).
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.2.3 Registers
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] Output Shift Register (OSR)
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] Holds data flowing from TX FIFO → pins/destinations.
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - PULL: Load 32-bit word from TX FIFO → OSR
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - OUT: Shift 1…32 bits from OSR → destination
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Autopull: Hardware auto-refills OSR when shift threshold reached
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Shift direction: Configurable left/right
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Example:* Stream bytes at 1 byte per 2 clocks:
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] .program pull_example
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] loop:
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5]     out pins, 8
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] pull
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5]     out pins, 8 [1]
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5]     out pins, 8 [1]
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5]     out pins, 8
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5]     jmp loop
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] With autopull enabled, simplifies to:
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] .program autopull_example
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] .wrap_target
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5]     out pins, 8 [1]
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] .wrap
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] Input Shift Register (ISR)
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] Holds data flowing from pins/sources → RX FIFO.
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - IN: Shift 1…32 bits from source → ISR
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - PUSH: Write ISR contents to RX FIFO (clears ISR to 0)
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Autopush: Hardware auto-pushes when shift threshold reached
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Shift direction: Configurable left/right
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Use:* Pad with zeroes after serial input:
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] in pins, 8      ; Shift in 8 data bits (LSB first)
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] in null, 24     ; Shift in 24 zero bits for alignment
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] push            ; Push to RX FIFO
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:42 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
