2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.4.2 JMP
2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Syntax:*
2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp <target>              ; Always jump
2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp !x <target>           ; Jump if X == 0
2026-05-15 13:30:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp x-- <target>          ; Jump if X != 0, then decrement
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp !y <target>           ; Jump if Y == 0
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp y-- <target>          ; Jump if Y != 0, then decrement
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp x!=y <target>         ; Jump if X != Y
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp pin <target>          ; Jump on EXECCTRL_JMP_PIN
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] jmp !osre <target>        ; Jump if OSR not empty
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Delays apply regardless* of condition outcome.
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.4.3 WAIT
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Syntax:*
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait <pol> gpio <gpio_num>              ; Wait on absolute GPIO
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait <pol> pin <pin_num>                ; Wait on IN-mapped pin
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait <pol> irq (prev|next) <irq_num>    ; Wait on IRQ flag
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait <pol> jmppin (+<offset>)           ; Wait on JMP pin
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Polarity:* 0 = wait for low, 1 = wait for high.
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Special IRQ behavior:*
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `wait 1 irq 0` clears flag 0 when condition met
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Flag indices support `rel` mode (relative to SM number)
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Stall timing: Delays begin after* condition is met.
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.4.4 IN
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Syntax:*
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] in <source>, <bit_count>
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Sources:*
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `pins` – IN-mapped GPIO pins
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `x`, `y` – Scratch registers
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `null` – Shift in zeroes (for alignment)
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `isr`, `osr` – Shift registers
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Autopush:* If enabled and ISR shift count ≥ threshold, push and clear.
2026-05-15 13:30:45 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
