2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.4.11 IRQ
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Syntax:*
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq (prev|next) set <n> (rel)     ; Set flag n
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq (prev|next) clear <n> (rel)   ; Clear flag n
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq (prev|next) wait <n> (rel)    ; Set and wait for clear
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq (prev|next) nowait <n> (rel)  ; Alias for 'set'
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Cross-PIO modes:*
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - (no prefix) – This PIO block
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `prev` – Next lower-numbered PIO (wraps)
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `next` – Next higher-numbered PIO (wraps)
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `rel` – Add SM number to flag index (mod 4 on 2 LSBs)
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Example (inter-SM sync):*
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] ; SM0
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq set 0 rel    ; Set flag (0 + 0) = flag 0
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait 1 irq 0 rel ; Wait on flag 0
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] ; SM1
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq set 0 rel    ; Set flag (0 + 1) = flag 1
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait 1 irq 0 rel ; Wait on flag 1
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.4.12 SET
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Syntax:*
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] set <destination>, <value>
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Destinations:*
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `pins` – Drive SET pins to value (0-31)
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `x`, `y` – Load into scratch registers (5 LSBs, rest cleared)
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `pindirs` – Set pin directions
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Typical use:* Loop counters, chip select, clock edges.
2026-05-15 13:30:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
