2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.5 Functional Details
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.5.1 Side-Set
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] Simultaneously changes GPIOs while executing main instruction.
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Benefits:*
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Precise timing (SPI clock + data edges)
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Compact code (no extra SET instruction)
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Independent pin mapping from OUT/SET
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Configuration:*
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Number of pins: `PINCTRLSIDESETCOUNT` (0-5)
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Enable bit optional: `EXECCTRLSIDEEN`
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Pin direction: `EXECCTRLSIDEPINDIR` (pins or pindirs)
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Base pin: `PINCTRLSIDESETBASE`
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Example: Fast SPI*
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] .program spi_tx_fast
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] .side_set 1
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] loop:
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5]     out pins, 1 side 0    ; Output data, clock low
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5]     jmp loop side 1       ; Jump, clock high
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 11.5.2 Program Wrapping
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] Eliminates JMP overhead via hardware loop.
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Syntax:*
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] .program squarewave_wrap
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] set pindirs, 1
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] .wrap_target
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5]     set pins, 1 [1]
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5]     set pins, 0 [1]
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] .wrap
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] • How it works:*
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. If PC matches WRAPTOP, jump to WRAPBOTTOM
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Else increment PC (wrap at 31)
2026-05-15 13:30:48 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. JMP still takes precedence
