2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Indexed RX FIFO Usage (greyline.pio confirmation)
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] Your `.fifo txget` directive is correct. The datasheet (11.4.9) confirms:
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] mov osr, rxfifo[y]        ; RP2350 v1 only
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] mov osr, rxfifo[<index>]  ; Index 0-3
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Requires:* `SHIFTCTRLFJOINRX_GET` set (pioasm handles this automatically).
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Your greyinit() issue: You're using `piosmputblocking()` to preload
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] patterns, but with `.fifo txget`, the system write goes to indexed RX FIFO storage*, not
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] the normal TX FIFO. The SDK may not expose the `RXF_PUTGET` registers directly.
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Fix (direct register access):*
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] // In grey_init(), replace the loop with:
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5]     pio->sm[sm].rxf_putget[i] = (uint32_t)pdm_patterns[i];
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] }
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] This assumes `rxf_putget` array exists in the SDK headers. If not, you'll need:
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] #define RXF_PUTGET(sm, idx) (pio_hw_t*)(pio0)->sm[sm].__base + 0x128 + (idx * 4)
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
