2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Timing Critique: greyline.pio
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] .program greyline
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] .fifo txget
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] set pindirs, 0           ; 1 cycle
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait 1 irq 6             ; 1+ cycles (stalls if IRQ not set)
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] mov y, pins              ; 1 cycle (reads GP46-47)
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] mov osr, rxfifo[y]       ; 1 cycle (indexed fetch)
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] out pindirs, 1           ; 6 times × 1 cycle = 6 cycles
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] set pindirs, 0           ; 1 cycle
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5]                          ; Total: ~10-12 cycles
2026-05-15 13:36:18 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Constraint: You have 10 cycles/pixel* (166.5 MHz / 10656 cycles per 64µs line).
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] - The 6 × `out pindirs, 1` instructions consume 6 cycles.
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `wait 1 irq 6` can stall, consuming extra cycles if IRQ6 is delayed.
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Risk: If IRQ6 isn't asserted every 10 cycles precisely, you'll slip timing.
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Recommendation:* Verify that `vidbit.pio` asserts IRQ6 with cycle-exact timing via `irq
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] set 6` in the active pixel region.
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:36:19 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
