2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. greyline.pio IRQ Dependency
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] // In grey_init()
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Issue:* greyline.pio waits on `irq 6`:
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] wait 1 irq 6
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] • But who sets IRQ6?* Looking at vidbit.pio:
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq set 6 [6]
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] irq clear 6
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Timing Risk:*
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] - IRQ6 is set/cleared in the active pixel region (per-pixel timing).
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] - greyline runs on PIO1, vidbit runs on PIO0.
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Cross-PIO IRQ propagation takes 1 cycle.
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] - If IRQ6 clears before greyline samples it, you'll stall forever.
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Verification needed:* Trace the exact IRQ6 timing. Consider adding debug output:
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] if (pio1->fdebug & (1 << PIO_FDEBUG_RXSTALL_LSB + GreyStateMachine)) {
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5]     printf("Grey SM stalled (likely IRQ6 timeout)\n");
2026-05-15 13:38:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] }
