2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Concern: This is a callback*, so it runs in ISR context. Spinning on
2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5] `getchartimeoutus(0)` in an ISR could block video timing.
2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Recommendation: Read only one character* per callback invocation:
2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5] void cdcReceiveCallback(void *user) {
2026-05-15 13:38:31 [claude-haiku-4-5]     int c = getchar_timeout_us(0);
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]     if (c == PICO_ERROR_TIMEOUT) return;
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]     if (c == 10) {
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]         uint32_t irq_status = spin_lock_blocking(line_lock);
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]         lines.push_back(std::string(buffer, charCount));
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]         spin_unlock(line_lock, irq_status);
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]         charCount = 0;
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]     } else {
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]         buffer[charCount++] = (char)c;
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]         if (charCount == 4096) charCount = 0;  // Prevent overflow
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5]     }
2026-05-15 13:38:32 [claude-haiku-4-5] }
