2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. PIO Clock Divider Configuration (chroma.pio)
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] ; Claims: clkdiv=9.3885 (PIO @ 17.734475MHz = 4x f_sc)
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Issue:* The comment states target frequency but the actual divider in C code:
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] pio_sm_set_clkdiv(pio,sm,2.3471f);  // chroma.pio line
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 9.3885 ≠ 2.3471* — these are inconsistent. If 166.5 MHz system clock, the math should be:
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Target: 4 × 4.43361875 MHz (PAL subcarrier × 4) = 17.734475 MHz
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Divisor: 166.5 / 17.734475 ≈ 9.388
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] The `2.3471` appears to be 166.5 / 71, which doesn't match PAL specs. Verify against actual
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] output.
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-15 14:03:08 [claude-haiku-4-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
