2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Interlace Mode (`LACE` define)
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] The code branches on `video_lace` to load either `progressiveFrame` or `evenFrame`/`oddFrame`. The
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] interlaced versions appear unfinished (only stubs in current files). Is the full interlace timing
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] implemented elsewhere?
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Teletext (WST) Integration
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] #ifdef WST
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]     wst_init(pio0, TeletextStateMachine);
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]     wst_dma_init(pio0, TeletextStateMachine);
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]     updateTeletextEven();  // Hamming 8/4 encoded
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] #endif
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] The Hamming encoding is correct, but the DMA channel configuration only supplies 15 words
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] per field. Is this intentional (partial line support), or should it be the full 385+ bits?
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. Serial Communication Callback
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] void cdcReceiveCallback(void *user) {
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]     int c = getchar_timeout_us(0);
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]     while (count-- && c != PICO_ERROR_TIMEOUT) {
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]         if(c==10) { /* push line */ }
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]         else { buffer[charCount++]=(char)c; }
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5]     }
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] }
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-16 10:18:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] The loop reads up to 3 characters per ISR fire. Is this sufficient for typical USB CDC baud rates,
2026-05-16 10:18:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] or should it drain the FIFO completely?
