2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5]  ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.6 ⛲  claude-haiku-4-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.002 4.678KB 4.71s
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] For Pico USB devices with CDC (Communications Device Class) support on Windows:
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 1. SetupAPI + Device Interface GUID*
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] Query `GUIDDEVINTERFACECOMPORT` to enumerate CDC virtual COM ports. Most direct approach
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] for CDC devices.
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 2. WMI Query*
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] Query `Win32SerialPort` filtered by `PNPDeviceID` containing "VID2E8A" (Raspberry Pi vendor
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] ID) and "PID_000A" (Pico CDC).
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 3. Registry SERIALCOMM*
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] `HKEYLOCALMACHINE\HARDWARE\DEVICEMAP\SERIALCOMM` lists active COM ports. Can
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] cross-reference with USB device tree.
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 4. libusb/libusbK*
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] Direct USB enumeration bypassing Windows CDC abstraction. Useful if you need raw USB control or
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] multiple Picos.
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • 5. EnumPorts API (Deprecated)*
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] Older but simpler; lists printer/serial ports though less detailed.
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Best for Pico CDC detection:*
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] • SetupAPI with `GUIDDEVINTERFACECOMPORT`* - finds the virtual COM port, can
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] extract USB device info, reliable for hotplug detection.
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] Alternatively, combining Registry SERIALCOMM with WMI device lookup gives you both
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] port names and USB identifiers without external dependencies.
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] What's your intended use - just discovery, or also port management/communication?
2026-05-17 08:52:04 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
