2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] `tudcdcwrite_flush()` is non-blocking - it just triggers the USB hardware to send queued
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] data.
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] The actual transmission happens asynchronously in the USB interrupt handler.
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] If you want truly non-blocking without flush, just call `tudcdcwrite()` and skip the flush
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] - data sits in the buffer until the next USB poll sends it.
2026-05-17 11:33:27 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
