2026-05-17 11:48:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] Impressive architecture. This is a sophisticated RP2350-based PAL video generator with multiple
2026-05-17 11:48:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] signal pipelines. Key observations:
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Signal Pipeline Architecture:*
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `pixelpump` → `onebit` → `threepin` chain creates component video
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Pixel bit-trains fed through state machine FIFO as waveform data
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] - 27 words × 32 bits = 864 pixel line width
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] - 10656 cycles/line @ 166.5 MHz = 64µs PAL line period ✓
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Novel Aspects:*
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Indexed RX FIFO (`mov osr, rxfifo[y]`) in `onebit.pio` — lookup table driven by pixel
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] state (GPIO46 loopback). This is RP2350 v1 exclusive.
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Tri-state output via `pindirs` in `threepin.pio` — elegant resistor DAC control (3 pins
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] = 8 levels per channel).
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. IRQ-gated line synchronisation — `wait 1 irq 0` keeps pipelines aligned across frames.
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-05-17 11:48:54 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Questions / Observations:*
