2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for sharing these files from the `pico-examples/pio` directory. They represent a standard
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] collection of Raspberry Pi Pico PIO (Programmable I/O) example projects, each demonstrating how to
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] implement various protocols and peripherals using PIO state machines.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] The examples cover a wide range of applications:
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Basic I/O: `hellopio`, `pioblink`, `squarewave` – simple output and timing.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Serial communication: `uarttx`, `uartrx`, `uart_dma` – software UART with
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] optional DMA and interrupt support.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - SPI: `spi` – full‑duplex SPI with multiple CPHA/CPOL modes and optional chip select.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - I2C: `i2c` – a PIO‑based I2C implementation with start/stop/repstart handling, bus
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] scanning, and blocking read/write.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - LED strips: `ws2812` and `ws2812_parallel` – driving WS2812 (NeoPixel) LEDs with
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] bit‑banged timing, including a parallel version.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Display: `st7789_lcd` – driving an ST7789 colour LCD via a simple serial interface.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - PWM and encoders: `pwm`, `quadratureencoder`, `quadratureencoder_substep` – PWM
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] generation and quadrature decoding with sub‑step interpolation.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Manchester encoding: `manchesterencoding`, `differentialmanchester` –
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] encoding/decoding Manchester and differential Manchester signals.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Clock‑synchronous input: `clocked_input` – reading serial data with an external clock.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Logic analyser: `logic_analyser` – using PIO with DMA to capture pin states at high
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] speed.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] - Miscellaneous: `addition` (PIO arithmetic), `apa102` (APA102 LED driver), `hub75` (RGB
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] matrix panel), `onewire`, `ir_nec`.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] Each subdirectory contains `.c` source, `.pio` assembly, `CMakeLists.txt`, and often a header or
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] readme. These are well‑known examples from the official Raspberry Pi Pico SDK and serve as a
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] reference for implementing custom PIO‑based peripherals.
2026-05-17 12:31:27 [deepseek-v4] 
