2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] This is the first time I have seen this particular project. It is a sophisticated, multi-layered
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] RP2350 video stack — significantly more involved than typical PIO VGA examples. A few observations
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] on what stands out, and a handful of items you may want to verify.
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] What is novel here
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] • RP2350 v1 PIO extensions used heavily. You are exploiting `FJOINRXGET` / `.fifo
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] txget` for hardware lookup tables in `greyline.pio` and `colorfifo.pio`. Using `mov osr, rxfifo[y]`
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] as a palette/PDM index is exactly the kind of thing the RP2350 datasheet hints at but few
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] implementations actually use.
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] • Multi-stage pixel pipeline. The `pixelpump → onebit → threepin` chain is an unusual
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] architecture. Decoupling the pixel source, bit-selector, and pin driver into separate state
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] machines lets you swap colour depths or output standards without rewriting the timing-critical
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] front end.
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] • PAL 576i with chroma in PIO. Generating the 4.43361875 MHz subcarrier (or 4× it at ~17.73
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] MHz) from a 166.5 MHz sysclk inside `chroma.pio` is ambitious. The 2-bit resistor DAC with a
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] reconstruction filter is a pragmatic low-parts-count approach.
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] • WST teletext injection. Doing World System Teletext encoding in the blanking interval —
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] including Hamming 8/4 and parity — is rare in hobby firmware. The `wst.pio` program is pleasingly
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] minimal.
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] Things worth a second look
2026-05-18 15:45:12 [kimi-k2.6] 
