2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6]     The file includes `<colorbit.h>`, which was not in the shared set. If it defines
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] `colorpumpinit`, `colorpumpdma_init`, and `colorTestAddress()`, everything is consistent;
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] otherwise the `#ifdef COLOR` block will not compile.
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] General architectural notes
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] • Your use of IRQ flags for horizontal sync lock between `vidbit.pio`, `greyline.pio`, and the
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] chroma pump is clean. On RP2350 you could also use `irq next` / `irq prev` if you ever need to
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] synchronise across PIO blocks, though keeping everything on `pio0`/`pio1` as you have done reduces
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] latency.
2026-05-18 15:45:13 [kimi-k2.6] • The `onebit.pio` approach of pushing the selected waveform back into an RX FIFO for `threepin` to
