2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] consumption rate.
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] In interlaced mode, you are pumping data at a specific cadence (likely synced to the field rate).
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] In progressive mode, the `vidbit` state machine is effectively consuming data at the same rate, but
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] if the DMA configuration or the frame buffer size is slightly off, the FIFO will starve.
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] Here are the most likely causes and how to diagnose them:
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
