2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] In `viddmainit`, you are using `channelconfigsetdreq(&c, pioget_dreq(pio0,
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] sm, true))`.
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] • The Issue: If your progressive frame buffer is larger than the interlace buffer, or if
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] the `dmachannelsettranscount` does not match the actual number of words the PIO
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] expects to consume per frame, the DMA will stop prematurely or get out of sync with the PIO's `wait
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1 irq 0` timing.
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Check: Verify that `progressiveWordCount` exactly matches the number of `out`
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] instructions the PIO executes per frame. If the PIO expects more words than the DMA provides, the
2026-05-18 19:00:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] FIFO will empty, and the state machine will stall (underrun).
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2. FIFO Join Mode
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] You are using `piosmsetfifojoin(&config, PIOFIFOJOIN_TX)`.
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] • The Issue: If you are using the same PIO block for both the `vidbit` program and other
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] tasks (like `wst` or `chroma`), joining the FIFOs gives you an 8-deep TX FIFO, but it disables
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] the RX FIFO.
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Check: If your `vidbit` program relies on `push` or `in` instructions, it will stall
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] immediately if the RX FIFO is disabled. Ensure that in progressive mode, you aren't accidentally
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] trying to push status/data back to a disabled RX FIFO.
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3. The "Line-End" Stall
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] The `vidbit.pio` program likely has a `jmp x--, line` or a `wait 1 irq 0` at the end of every line.
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] • The Issue: If the DMA transfer isn't perfectly aligned to the line count, the DMA will be
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] "ahead" or "behind" the PIO. In interlace, the field-based `vid_fieldi` might be masking this by
2026-05-18 19:00:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] resetting the DMA on every field. In progressive, if you are running a continuous stream, any
