2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] Minimalist Passive Alternative
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] If you prefer not to use an op-amp, this divider directly biases and attenuates the signal. The
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] trade-off is a higher source impedance (~300 kΩ) into the ADC, so you should sample more slowly or
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] allow extra acquisition time.
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] Guitar ----+---- C1 ---- Rs ----+---- Rlimit ----> Pico ADC
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] (RCA tip)  |   100nF   1M      |    10k
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]           Rgnd                R1
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]           1M                 1M
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]            |                  |
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]           GND                 +---- R2
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]                                 1M
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]                                  |
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6]                                 GND
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] Clamp diodes and 100pF cap to GND at the ADC pin (same as above).
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] • How it works*
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] • Rgnd (1 MΩ) again gives the guitar its DC reference.
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] • Rs, R1, R2 (all 1 MΩ) form an attenuator: the ADC node sees one-third of the guitar
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] voltage riding on a 1.65 V bias.
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] • Rlimit (10 kΩ) and the BAT54 clamp pair protect the Pico pin.
2026-05-25 15:26:05 [kimi-k2.6] 
