2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] Perfect — 4.7k is useful here.
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] Use it like this for RCA line-in:
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] - GPIO/PIO pin → 330 Ω → 4.7k → series coupling capacitor (1–10 µF) → RCA
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] tip
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Pico GND → RCA sleeve
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] That will greatly tame level/current and make the TV input happier.
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] If volume is too low, reduce total series resistance (e.g. remove 4.7k).
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] If too high/distorted, increase it (or add another resistor).
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-05-26 20:25:24 [gpt-5.3-codex] And yes, your resistor type/power rating is fine — audio line currents here are tiny.
